def leave_a_review_page():
    """/leave-a-review/ - removes the friction that stops older customers reviewing.

    The bottleneck is not willingness, it is that many have never left a Google review
    and do not know a Google account is required. This page shows them, plainly.
    Also gives the team a short URL to say on the phone and print on the QR card.

    RULES (do not regress): the ask is UNCONDITIONAL - never route unhappy customers
    away from Google before asking (that is review gating, against Google policy) - and
    NO incentive is ever offered for a review (unlawful in the UK, DMCC Act). Service
    recovery is offered AFTER the ask. The referral offer is a separate thing entirely.
    """
    info_page(
        slug="leave-a-review",
        crumb_name="Leave a Review",
        title="Leave Us a Google Review | 365 Techies, Bournemouth",
        og_title="Leave 365 Techies a Google review",
        eyebrow="// THANK YOU",
        h1='Leave us a <em class="grad grad--green">Google review</em>',
        lede="If we&rsquo;ve helped you, thirty seconds of your time genuinely changes who finds us next. Here&rsquo;s the button &mdash; and, if you&rsquo;ve never left one before, exactly how it works.",
        desc="Leave a Google review for 365 Techies in Bournemouth. One button, about thirty seconds - plus a plain-English guide for anyone who has never left a Google review before.",
        chips=["About 30 seconds", "Rated 4.9 on Google", "We read every one"],
        hero_cta1=("Leave a Google review", 'https://search.google.com/local/writereview?placeid=ChIJlTb8YRuic0gRCRczduB8OFI'),
        hero_cta2=("Call 01202 775566", "tel:+441202775566"),
        pre=_LEAVE_REVIEW_PRE,
        inner='          <h2>Never left a Google review before? Here&rsquo;s exactly what happens</h2>\n          <p>Plenty of people have never written one, and there&rsquo;s nothing obvious about it. Here is the whole process, honestly, with no surprises.</p>\n          <ol>\n            <li><strong>You press the button above.</strong> A Google page opens showing our name, 365 Techies, and a row of five stars.</li>\n            <li><strong>You&rsquo;ll need to be signed in to a Google account.</strong> If you use Gmail, or an Android phone, you already have one &mdash; it may sign you in automatically. If it asks you to sign in, that&rsquo;s Google checking you&rsquo;re a real person, not us asking for anything.</li>\n            <li><strong>Tap the number of stars</strong> you think we deserve. Five stars is the top.</li>\n            <li><strong>Write a line or two</strong> in the box. It genuinely doesn&rsquo;t need to be long &mdash; &ldquo;Steve sorted my laptop the same day and explained everything clearly&rdquo; is a perfect review.</li>\n            <li><strong>Press Post.</strong> It appears on our Google listing within a few minutes. Your first name and Google profile picture show alongside it.</li>\n          </ol>\n\n          <h2>&ldquo;I don&rsquo;t have a Google account&rdquo;</h2>\n          <p>Then honestly, don&rsquo;t worry about it &mdash; please don&rsquo;t go creating one just for us. Google reviews can only be left by people with a Google account, and that&rsquo;s their rule, not ours.</p>\n          <p>If you&rsquo;d still like to say something kind, you&rsquo;re very welcome to <a href="https://www.facebook.com/365computersuk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">leave a recommendation on our Facebook page</a>, or simply ring us on <a href="tel:+441202775566">01202&nbsp;775566</a> and tell us. It won&rsquo;t appear on Google, but it means a great deal to hear it.</p>\n\n          <h2>Why we ask &mdash; the honest version</h2>\n          <p>We don&rsquo;t advertise much. Most of our customers come from someone recommending us, or from finding us on Google when their computer has gone wrong. When somebody in Wimborne or Blandford searches for computer help at nine o&rsquo;clock at night, what decides whether they find us is largely what other local people have said.</p>\n          <p>So a review from you genuinely helps a stranger find a firm that will answer the phone. That&rsquo;s the whole of it.</p>\n          <p><strong>We read every single one</strong> &mdash; both of us. And we&rsquo;d rather have an honest three stars telling us where we fell short than a polite five that doesn&rsquo;t help us improve. We never offer anything in return for a review, because paying for reviews is both against Google&rsquo;s rules and unlawful in the UK &mdash; and because a review you were paid for isn&rsquo;t worth reading.</p>\n\n          <h2>If something wasn&rsquo;t right</h2>\n          <p>Please tell us before anything else. Ring <a href="tel:+441202775566">01202&nbsp;775566</a> or <a href="/contact/">drop us a line</a> and we&rsquo;ll put it right &mdash; that&rsquo;s the point of using a small family firm rather than a call centre. You&rsquo;re still welcome to leave whatever review you think is fair afterwards; we&rsquo;d just rather fix the problem first.</p>\n\n          <h2>Recommending us to someone instead?</h2>\n          <p>That&rsquo;s worth even more to us than a review. If you know somebody battling their computer, their first Computer Service &amp; Health Check is on us and you get a month free on your support plan &mdash; just ask them to mention your name. Here&rsquo;s <a href="/refer-a-friend/">how it works</a>.</p>',
        faqs=[
            ("Do I need a Google account?", "Yes &mdash; that is Google&rsquo;s rule for all reviews, not ours. If you use Gmail or an Android phone you already have one. If you don&rsquo;t, please don&rsquo;t create one just for us; ring us instead, or leave a recommendation on our Facebook page."),
            ("How long does it take?", "About thirty seconds. Tap the stars, write a line, press Post. It really doesn&rsquo;t need to be long &mdash; a single honest sentence is a perfect review."),
            ("Will my name show?", "Your Google account&rsquo;s first name and profile picture appear with the review. There is no way to leave a Google review anonymously."),
            ("Can I change or delete it later?", "Yes. Open Google Maps, tap your profile picture, choose &ldquo;Your contributions&rdquo; and you can edit or delete any review you&rsquo;ve left, at any time."),
            ("Do you offer anything for leaving a review?", "No, and we never will. Rewarding reviews is against Google&rsquo;s rules and unlawful in the UK. We do thank people who recommend us to a friend, which is a completely separate thing."),
            ("Something wasn&rsquo;t right &mdash; what should I do?", "Ring us on 01202 775566 first and we&rsquo;ll put it right. You&rsquo;re still welcome to leave whatever review you feel is fair; we&rsquo;d just rather fix the problem than read about it."),
        ],
        cta_args=("Thank you &mdash; genuinely",
                  "Every review is read by both of us, and it is how other local people find a firm that answers the phone.",
                  ("Leave a Google review", 'https://search.google.com/local/writereview?placeid=ChIJlTb8YRuic0gRCRczduB8OFI'),
                  ("Read our reviews", "/reviews/")),
    )
leave_a_review_page()

